# Kang, Suspicious Captain: entering on turn 3, it goads itself and the creature an opponent controls that it chose
# (CR 701.15a) for as long as its controller controls it (CR 611.2b): both show GoadedBy Bot1, and Kang is summoning sick,
# so it cannot attack that turn. A goaded creature attacks each combat if able and attacks a player other than the goader's
# controller if able (CR 701.15b): Bot2's goaded Llanowar Elves must attack Bot1 on turn 4 - that attack is "one or more
# goaded creatures attack" (CR 508.1, 603.2c), firing Kang's ability even though Bot1 is not the attacking player - and
# Kang itself must attack on turn 5. Each attack puts one +1/+1 counter on a creature Bot1 controls (Kang), one per combat
# and not one per goaded creature: one after turn 4, two after turn 5. Kang is no creature an opponent controls, so its own
# entry ability cannot target it; Ornithopter is Bot2's second creature, so the choice is offered and a refusal taken first.

